# Package management — pnpm

This monorepo uses **pnpm** exclusively.

## Do

- `pnpm install` at repo root (workspaces).
- `pnpm --filter <package> <script>` or `pnpm -C frontend|backend <script>` for package-scoped commands.
- Add dependencies with `pnpm add` / `pnpm add -D` from the correct package directory or via `--filter`.
- Set `packageManager` in root `package.json` when the workspace exists (e.g. `pnpm@9.x`).

## Do not

- Use `npm install`, `npm run`, `yarn`, or `npx` for project dependency management (use `pnpm exec` / `pnpm dlx` when a one-off CLI is needed).
- Add `package-lock.json` or `yarn.lock`; use **`pnpm-lock.yaml`** only.

## Documentation

README and CI must document pnpm commands, not npm/yarn equivalents.
